{%- comment -%}
  Bundle Builder — interactive "build your box" section (Model B, multi-box).

  The shopper mixes flavours freely via per-flavour steppers. The packs are
  auto-chunked into boxes of BOX_CAPACITY (6) in add order; the total must be a
  multiple of 6 (no half-built box) before "Add to cart" unlocks. Each full box
  is added to the native Shopify cart as its own "Build Your Box" line item at
  the flat box price — boxes with an identical flavour mix merge into one line
  with quantity N. No discount tiers.

  Two standalone web components, communicating only via `bundle-v2:updated` on
  `document` (theme convention — see conventions/sections.md):

    <bundle-v2-builder> (assets/bundle-v2-builder.js)
      Owns the draft (flat ordered list of packs, no upper limit)
      + its localStorage persistence, the per-flavour steppers, the divisible-by-4
      gate, and "Add to cart". Reads the .bundle-v2-flavours JSON blob below for
      flavour name/notes/image.

    <bundle-v2-stage> (assets/bundle-v2-stage.js)
      The pack strip inside the "Your box" panel. Pure 2D (NO three.js). Listens
      for `bundle-v2:updated` and renders one horizontal row of pouches side by
      side in add order, newest at the right. Unlike v1 there is NO carton
      artwork — see BOX IMAGERY below. The row is cloned from a <template>; pack
      images ride along in the event detail.

  LAYOUT. Flavour cards (photo from the flavour's `meal_image`, name +
  descriptor, "Add +" bar that becomes a − qty + stepper) fill the left; the
  yellow "Your box" panel (strip, subscription choice, add to cart) is sticky on
  the right at >=900px and stacks after the cards below that.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DATA MODEL

  The box itself is ONE product (the "Build Your Box" product, priced at the
  flat box price) chosen in the section settings. On "Add to cart" the section
  POSTs one item per full box to /cart/add.js (with the box's flavours as
  line-item properties) — the native cart treats each as any other line item.

  Flavours are CURATED PER BOX PRODUCT: the box product's
  `custom.included_flavours` metafield (a list of `flavour` metaobjects) sets
  which flavours show and in what order. Each referenced flavour metaobject
  needs these field handles:

    name        single_line_text_field  — flavour name ("Mexi Fiesta Blend")
    atrributes  single_line_text_field  — descriptors ("Smoky • Rich • Peppery") (optional)
                                          (field-handle typo lives in Shopify; rename
                                          there to `attributes` and update this file)
    image       file_reference (image)   — the pouch render PNG for the visualiser
    sku         single_line_text_field  — the single-pack SKU, mirrored from the
                                          flavour's product variant. Stored here (NOT
                                          read from product_reference.value.variants)
                                          because the single-pack products are excluded
                                          from the Online Store channel, and Liquid
                                          cannot reach an off-channel product's variants
                                          via a metafield reference — the SKU collapses
                                          to "". The 3PL consumes this via the hidden
                                          `_bundle` line-item property, so it must be set.

  No box product (or an empty metafield) → no flavours render and add stays off.

  BOX IMAGERY — deliberately absent in v2. Where v1 composites the packs between
  a box-back and box-front render, this section draws the pack images alone. The
  strip sizes each slot to the render's own aspect (--pack-ratio in the
  stylesheet) — the renders come from the flavour's `v2_pack_render`.
  While the draft is empty the stage carries `.is-empty` and a centred prompt
  (`sections.bundle_builder.empty_custom_box`) shows in its place, so the strip
  never renders blank. The box-back/box-front image settings and the
  assets/box-back.png / box-front.png fallbacks are v1-only — don't reintroduce
  them here.

  PACKS ARE SOLD INDIVIDUALLY. There is no box quantum and no upper limit — the
  only constraint is an order MINIMUM of 6 packs, locked here (not a merchant
  setting). Above the minimum any quantity is addable.

  The box product's variant price must therefore be the SINGLE-PACK price; the
  whole draft goes to the cart as one line with quantity = the pack count. v1 is
  the older model — priced per box of 4, one line per full box — so the two
  sections are NOT interchangeable and their products are priced differently.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign min_packs = 6 -%}
{%- assign box_product = section.settings.box_product -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Prefer the available variant (for price + a clean add); fall back to the first
  variant so the add button stays live even when nothing is "available" — the
  /cart/add.js call then surfaces a real "out of stock" error instead of the
  button silently sitting disabled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign box_variant = box_product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: box_product.variants.first -%}
{%- comment -%} Curated, ordered list of flavour metaobjects, set per box product. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign included_flavours = box_product.metafields.custom.included_flavours.value -%}

<bundle-v2-builder
  class="bundle-v2-builder{% if section.settings.full_screen %} full-screen{% endif %}"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  data-min-packs="{{ min_packs }}"
  {% if box_variant %}data-box-variant-id="{{ box_variant.id }}"{% endif %}
  {%- comment -%} Per-PACK price — the variant price is the single-pack price. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if box_variant %}data-box-price-cents="{{ box_variant.price }}"{% endif %}
  data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format }}"
  data-i18n-add="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_to_cart' | t }}"
  {%- comment -%} v2 counts up to the order minimum, not to a full box — its own key. {%- endcomment -%}
  data-i18n-add-more="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_minimum' | t }}"
  data-i18n-added="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.added' | t: product: box_product.title }}"
  data-i18n-error="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.checkout_error' | t }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    Visible line-item property stamped on every blend line, marking it as part of
    the custom box. Visible (no leading underscore) so it carries through cart,
    checkout and the order confirmation; it is also what the cart groups on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-box-property-key="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.box_property_key' | t }}"
  data-box-property-value="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.box_property_value' | t }}"
>
  <script type="application/json" class="bundle-v2-flavours">
    [
      {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Each flavour must resolve to a PURCHASABLE variant — v2 adds the blends
          themselves to the cart, one line each, rather than a single box line.

          These are the real single-pack products, via the flavour metaobject's
          `product_reference`. NOTE they must be published to the ONLINE STORE
          sales channel: while they aren't, Liquid sees the reference as blank,
          `variantId` comes through null, and add-to-cart stays disabled — the
          section degrades rather than posting a variant /cart/add.js would
          reject. (A dev stand-in that borrowed the published Box products lived
          here until 2026-08-26; see git history if it's needed again.)
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign flavour_product = flavour.product_reference.value -%}
        {%- assign flavour_variant = flavour_product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: flavour_product.variants.first -%}
        {
          "id": {{ flavour.system.handle | json }},
          "name": {{ flavour.name.value | json }},
          "attributes": {{ flavour.atrributes.value | default: '' | json }},
          "image": {% if flavour.v2_pack_render.value != blank %}{{ flavour.v2_pack_render.value | image_url: width: 600 | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %},
          "sku": {{ flavour.sku.value | default: '' | json }},
          {%- comment -%} `| append: ''` casts the colour object to its hex string; `| json` alone rejects it. {%- endcomment -%}
          "colour": {{ flavour.dark_colour | append: '' | json }},
          "variantId": {% if flavour_variant %}{{ flavour_variant.id | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
          "priceCents": {% if flavour_variant %}{{ flavour_variant.price }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
          {%- comment -%}
            Each blend's OWN selling plans. A selling plan id is only valid for
            variants in its own group, and Recharge may well have made a separate
            group per product — so the plan is matched across blends by NAME and
            each line is posted with its own id. Never reuse one blend's id for
            another, and never reuse the box product's.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          "plans": [
            {%- for allocation in flavour_variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
              {
                "name": {{ allocation.selling_plan.name | json }},
                "id": {{ allocation.selling_plan.id | json }},
                "priceCents": {{ allocation.price }},
                "compareCents": {{ allocation.compare_at_price | default: allocation.price }}
              }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  </script>

  <div class="bundle-v2-layout">
    <div class="bundle-v2-selection">
      <header class="section-lockup">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <h1 class="text-h1">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</h1>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="text-h3">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>

      <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-list" data-flavour-list>
        {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
          <article
            class="bundle-v2-flavour"
            data-flavour-card
            data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
          >
            {%- comment -%} Card photo is the flavour's `meal_image`, not the pack render. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if flavour.meal_image.value != blank -%}
              <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-media">
                {{ flavour.meal_image.value | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '300, 400, 600, 800',
                  sizes: '(min-width: 900px) 22vw, 45vw',
                  alt: flavour.name.value
                }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
            <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-body">
              <h3 class="text-ui">{{ flavour.name }}</h3>
              {%- if flavour.v2_description != blank -%}
                <p class="bundle-v2-flavour-attributes text-body">{{ flavour.v2_description }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-action">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="bundle-v2-add-blend text-h1"
                data-action="add"
                data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.increase' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
              >
                {{- 'products.product.add' | t -}}
              </button>

              <div class="bundle-v2-stepper">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  data-action="remove"
                  data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
                  aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.decrease' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
                >
                  <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 7 1" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M0 1V0H7V1H0Z"/>
                  </svg>
                </button>
                <span class="bundle-v2-qty text-h1" data-qty="{{ flavour.system.handle }}" aria-live="polite">0</span>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  data-action="add"
                  data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
                  aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.increase' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
                >
                  <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 7 7" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M3 4H0V3H3V0H4V3H7V4H4V7H3V4Z"/>
                  </svg>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="text-body">{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.no_flavours' | t }}</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bundle-v2-panel-column">
    <aside class="bundle-v2-panel is-collapsed"{% if section.settings.panel_title != blank %} aria-labelledby="bundle-v2-panel-title-{{ section.id }}"{% endif %}>
      <header class="bundle-v2-panel-header">
        <div class="bundle-v2-panel-heading">
          {%- if section.settings.panel_title != blank -%}
            <h2 class="text-h1" id="bundle-v2-panel-title-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.panel_title }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Mobile only (hidden from 900px): the panel is pinned to the bottom of the
            screen there and starts collapsed to just the frequency + add to cart.
            The arrow points up while collapsed and flips when open.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="bundle-v2-panel-toggle"
            data-panel-toggle
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-label="{{ 'products.product.details' | t }}"
          >
            <svg width="18" height="9" viewBox="0 0 18 9" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M18 9L0 9L0 7L18 7V9ZM14 5L4 5L9 0L14 5Z" fill="currentColor"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        {%- if section.settings.panel_subtitle != blank -%}
          <p class="bundle-v2-panel-subtitle text-body">{{ section.settings.panel_subtitle }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>

      <bundle-v2-stage class="bundle-v2-stage">
        <div class="bundle-v2-stage-track" data-stage></div>
        {%- comment -%}
          The single row of pouches, cloned from this template by bundle-v2-stage.js.
          Packs sit side by side in add order and never wrap — the track scrolls
          instead, pinned to the newest pack. The element is an empty frame; the
          stage appends the pack slots.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <template data-box-template>
          <div class="bundle-v2-row" data-scene></div>
        </template>

        {%- comment -%}
          Shown while the draft is empty; bundle-v2-stage.js toggles `.is-empty` on
          the host. Overlays the reserved strip rather than replacing it, so
          nothing reflows when the first pack lands.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="bundle-v2-empty text-body">{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.empty_custom_box' | t }}</p>
      </bundle-v2-stage>

      <footer class="bundle-v2-footer">
        {%- comment -%}
          Subscription control. Built from the BLENDS, not the box — the box is no
          longer purchased, and its plan ids would be rejected on a blend line.

          The frequency list comes from the first flavour that has plans; on
          add-to-cart bundle-v2-builder.js looks the chosen frequency up by NAME
          in each blend's own plan list, so every line carries a plan id valid for
          its own variant. A frequency not offered by every blend is dropped from
          the list by the JS.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign plan_source = blank -%}
        {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
          {%- assign candidate = flavour.product_reference.value -%}
          {%- assign candidate_variant = candidate.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: candidate.variants.first -%}
          {%- if candidate_variant.selling_plan_allocations.size > 0 -%}
            {%- assign plan_source = candidate_variant -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          DESIGN PLACEHOLDER. With no real plans and `preview_subscription` ticked,
          the block renders with dummy frequencies so the layout can be reviewed
          before Loop is attached. It is inert: the dummy frequencies match no
          blend's plan list, so planFor() finds nothing and the order is added as a
          plain one-time purchase. Real plans always win over the placeholder.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign is_placeholder = false -%}
        {%- if plan_source == blank and section.settings.preview_subscription -%}
          {%- assign is_placeholder = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if plan_source != blank or is_placeholder -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            LOOP SEAM. Everything the subscription needs from the page is here:
            the [data-sub-mode] radios, the [data-sub-select] frequency list and the
            per-blend `plans` in the flavours JSON above. bundle-v2-builder.js reads
            only those (planName / planFor). Wiring Loop in means changing what feeds
            them — not the layout.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="bundle-v2-subscription" data-subscription{% if is_placeholder %} data-placeholder{% endif %}>
            <fieldset class="bundle-v2-sub-options">
              <legend class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.purchase_options' | t }}</legend>

              <label class="bundle-v2-sub-option is-selected">
                <input type="radio" name="bundle-v2-purchase-{{ section.id }}" value="subscription" checked data-sub-mode>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-label text-ui">{{ section.settings.subscribe_label }}<span class="bundle-v2-sub-note"> {{ section.settings.subscribe_note }}</span></span>
                {%- comment -%} Filled by bundle-v2-builder.js updateAddPrice(): original total struck through, then the subscription total. {%- endcomment -%}
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-price text-ui">
                  <s data-sub-was hidden></s>
                  <span data-sub-price></span>
                </span>
              </label>

              <div class="bundle-v2-sub-details" data-sub-frequency>
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="bundle-v2-frequency-{{ section.id }}">{{ 'products.product.deliver_every' | t }}</label>
                <div class="bundle-v2-sub-select-wrap">
                  <select id="bundle-v2-frequency-{{ section.id }}" class="bundle-v2-sub-select text-ui" data-sub-select>
                    {%- comment -%} value is the plan NAME — the key that maps across blends. {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- if is_placeholder -%}
                      <option value="placeholder-1">1 month</option>
                      <option value="placeholder-2">2 months</option>
                      <option value="placeholder-3">3 months</option>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- for allocation in plan_source.selling_plan_allocations -%}
                        <option value="{{ allocation.selling_plan.name | escape }}">
                          {{ allocation.selling_plan.name | split: ' subscription' | first }}
                        </option>
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </select>
                  <svg class="bundle-v2-sub-chevron" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M2 4l4 4 4-4"/>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <ul class="bundle-v2-sub-benefits text-body">
                  {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
                    {%- case i -%}
                      {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign benefit = section.settings.benefit_1 -%}
                      {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign benefit = section.settings.benefit_2 -%}
                      {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign benefit = section.settings.benefit_3 -%}
                    {%- endcase -%}
                    {%- if benefit != blank -%}
                      <li>{% render 'icon-check-circle' %}<span>{{ benefit }}</span></li>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <label class="bundle-v2-sub-option">
                <input type="radio" name="bundle-v2-purchase-{{ section.id }}" value="onetime" data-sub-mode>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-label text-ui">{{ 'products.product.one_time' | t }}</span>
              </label>
            </fieldset>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <button type="button" class="button bundle-v2-add" data-add disabled>
          <span class="bundle-v2-add-inner">
            <span class="bundle-v2-add-main">
              <span class="bundle-v2-add-label" data-add-label>{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_to_cart' | t }}</span>
              {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'bundle-v2-add-icon' %}
            </span>
            {%- if box_variant -%}
              {%- comment -%} Empty-state preview: the minimum order, matching updateAddPrice(). {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="bundle-v2-add-price">{{ box_variant.price | times: min_packs | money }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </button>

        <p class="bundle-v2-hint text-body" data-hint aria-live="polite"></p>

        <div class="form-error" data-error role="alert" hidden></div>
      </footer>
    </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</bundle-v2-builder>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bundle-v2-builder {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Phones-only: bump top/bottom for a touch more vertical breathing room. */
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder {
      padding-block: var(--spacing-m);
    }
  }

  /* Two columns on desktop: the flavour grid, then the sticky "Your box" panel.
     Stacked on mobile/tablet with the panel after the cards. */
  .bundle-v2-layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-m);
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-l);
  }

  .bundle-v2-selection {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-m);
    min-width: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .bundle-v2-selection > .section-lockup h2 {
    max-width: 36ch;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  /* Flavour card: photo, name + descriptor, then one full-width action bar that
     is either "Add +" or the − qty + stepper. */
  .bundle-v2-flavour {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Extra room under the photo — with the card's own gap that makes the photo →
     name spacing --spacing-s (16px). */
  .bundle-v2-flavour-media {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-media img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-body {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-body h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-attributes {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-action {
    display: flex;
    /* Extra room above the action bar — with the card's own gap that makes
       description → button --spacing-s (16px), at every width. */
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  /* Dark bar, same shape and type as .button but brand dark — the same
     dark-variant precedent as .bundle-v2-add below. */
  .bundle-v2-add-blend {
    flex: 1;
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs) var(--spacing-xs) calc(var(--spacing-xxs) - 2px);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add-blend:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper {
    flex: 1;
    display: none;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: var(--spacing-xxxs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour.is-active .bundle-v2-add-blend {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour.is-active .bundle-v2-stepper {
    display: flex;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper button {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    padding: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper button:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .bundle-v2-qty {
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* "Your box" panel — brand yellow, sticky beside the grid on desktop. */
  .bundle-v2-panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-panel-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-panel-header h2 {
    margin: 0;
    /* The panel is yellow, so the grey eyebrow colour would fail contrast. */
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-panel-subtitle {
    margin: 0;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, var(--color-accent));
  }

  /* Footer: subscription choice, add button, hint. */
  .bundle-v2-footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 15%, var(--color-accent));
  }

  /* Dark variant of the primary .button (same shape and type). Muted until the
     minimum is met, then brand dark. */
  .bundle-v2-add {
    width: 100%;
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 40%, var(--color-accent));
    color: var(--color-bg);
    transition:
      background-color var(--transition-fast),
      color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add:not(:disabled) {
    background-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add:not(:disabled):hover {
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Override .button:disabled's 0.6 opacity — the muted bg does the "not yet"
     signalling on its own. */
  .bundle-v2-add:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* Inner flex wrapper — keep .button as inline-block per the convention; flex
     an inner span when an icon + label need laying out side-by-side. */
  .bundle-v2-add-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add-main {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add-price {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* 2px of padding-bottom nudges the arrow up to optically align with the
     cap-line of the all-caps label. */
  .bundle-v2-add-icon {
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }

  /* Minimum-order hint. Empty until the shopper starts building. */
  .bundle-v2-hint {
    margin: 0;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 65%, var(--color-accent));
  }

  .bundle-v2-hint:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-panel-heading {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-panel-toggle {
    flex: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 32px;
    height: 24px;
    margin-left: auto;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Open: the arrow flips. */
  .bundle-v2-panel:not(.is-collapsed) .bundle-v2-panel-toggle svg {
    rotate: 180deg;
  }

  /* Subscribe row: label on the left, totals on the right. */
  .bundle-v2-sub-price {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-price s {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, var(--color-accent));
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-price s[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The "(10% off)" note only stands in for the benefits list while collapsed. */
  .bundle-v2-sub-note {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Mobile + tablet: the panel is pinned to the bottom of the screen with the
     small inset the section already has at the sides. Sticky rather than fixed,
     so it pins while the cards scroll but lands at the end of the section
     instead of covering the site footer (body uses overflow-x: clip, which
     keeps sticky working). Below the header's z-index (9), above the cards. */
  @media (max-width: 899.98px) {
    .bundle-v2-panel-column {
      position: sticky;
      bottom: var(--spacing-xxs);
      z-index: 8;
      /* The builder pads its sides by xs; pull the panel out to an xxs inset so it
         sits closer to the screen edge than the cards do. */
      margin-inline: calc(var(--spacing-xxs) - var(--spacing-xs));
    }

    /* Keep the open panel reachable on short screens. */
    .bundle-v2-panel {
      max-height: calc(100dvh - var(--spacing-xl));
      overflow-y: auto;
    }

    /* Collapsed: just the subscribe row, the frequency dropdown, one time and
       add to cart. The pack strip and the benefits list are hidden. */
    .bundle-v2-panel.is-collapsed .bundle-v2-stage,
    .bundle-v2-panel.is-collapsed .bundle-v2-sub-benefits {
      display: none;
    }

    .bundle-v2-panel.is-collapsed .bundle-v2-sub-details {
      padding: 0;
      background-color: transparent;
    }

    .bundle-v2-panel.is-collapsed .bundle-v2-sub-note {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  /* Pack strip. Side by side in add order, newest at the right, never wrapping;
     the track scrolls (drag, trackpad or touch) and stays pinned to the newest
     pack. Each slot is the v2_pack_render's own shape (tight-cropped, portrait,
     ~600:770) with height set here; re-check --pack-ratio if the renders are
     re-exported at a different aspect. */
  .bundle-v2-stage {
    /* Pouches are sized off the strip's own width so it always fits 4½ of them:
       the half-visible pack at the left edge shows there's more to scroll to,
       whatever the panel width. */
    --pack-visible: 4.5;
    --pack-width: calc((100cqw - (var(--pack-visible) - 0.5) * var(--spacing-xxs)) / var(--pack-visible));
    --pack-ratio: 600 / 770;
    display: block;
    container-type: inline-size;
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    /* Keeps the pack z-indexes local so they can't paint over the cart drawer. */
    isolation: isolate;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage-track {
    display: block;
    overflow-x: auto;
    /* overflow-x: auto forces overflow-y to auto too; the enter/exit transforms
       would otherwise flash a vertical scrollbar. */
    overflow-y: hidden;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    cursor: grab;
    padding-block: var(--spacing-xxs);
    min-height: calc(var(--pack-width) * 770 / 600 + var(--spacing-xxs) * 2);
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage-track::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage.is-dragging .bundle-v2-stage-track {
    cursor: grabbing;
    user-select: none;
  }

  /* Empty state — centred over the reserved strip. */
  .bundle-v2-empty {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, var(--color-accent));
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage:not(.is-empty) .bundle-v2-empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    /* Packs pin to the right when the row is narrower than the track. */
    justify-content: flex-end;
    width: max-content;
    min-width: 100%;
  }

  .bundle-v2-slot {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: var(--pack-width);
    aspect-ratio: var(--pack-ratio);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-pack {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 8px var(--color-shadow-soft));
    transition: transform 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), opacity 0.32s ease;
  }

  .bundle-v2-slot.is-entering .bundle-v2-pack {
    transform: translateY(-12%);
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-slot.is-leaving .bundle-v2-pack {
    transform: translateY(-8%);
    opacity: 0;
    transition-duration: 0.18s;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder {
      padding: var(--spacing-m);
    }

    .bundle-v2-layout {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: var(--spacing-m);
    }

    /* Cards take a fixed two-column block. The panel column fills the rest and
       is as tall as the grid; auto margins centre the panel both ways within it,
       and sticky keeps it in view while the grid scrolls past. */
    .bundle-v2-selection {
      flex: 0 1 640px;
    }

    .bundle-v2-panel-column {
      flex: 1;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    /* Pinned in the vertical middle of the window while the section is on screen
       (--panel-h is the panel's own height, kept current by bundle-v2-stage.js),
       then it scrolls away with the page as the section ends. Never closer to the
       top than --spacing-l if the panel is taller than the window. */
    .bundle-v2-panel {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 370px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      position: sticky;
      top: max(var(--spacing-l), calc((100vh - var(--panel-h, 480px)) / 2));
    }

    /* The collapse toggle is a mobile control. */
    .bundle-v2-panel-toggle {
      display: none;
    }

    /* Full-screen toggle (in section settings): adds extra vertical breathing
       room above and below the builder on desktop. Steps up at 1500px. */
    .bundle-v2-builder.full-screen {
      padding-top: var(--spacing-l);
      padding-bottom: var(--spacing-l);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1500px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder.full-screen {
      padding-top: var(--spacing-xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bundle-v2-pack,
    .bundle-v2-add-blend,
    .bundle-v2-stepper button {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  /* Subscription control. */
  .bundle-v2-subscription {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-options {
    border: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input[type="radio"] {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: transparent;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input:checked ~ .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    background-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input:focus-visible ~ .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-label {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }

  /* Frequency + benefits, in a slightly darker yellow well under the option. */
  .bundle-v2-sub-details {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 8%, var(--color-accent));
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-details[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-select-wrap {
    position: relative;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs) var(--spacing-m) var(--spacing-xxs) var(--spacing-xxs);
    color: var(--color-text);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 12%, var(--color-accent));
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    appearance: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-chevron {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: var(--spacing-xxs);
    translate: 0 -50%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-benefits {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-benefits li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-benefits svg {
    flex: none;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bundle-v2-sub-box {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

<script type="module" src="{{ 'bundle-v2-builder.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
<script type="module" src="{{ 'bundle-v2-stage.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

